cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this archive, please cite the accompanying paper (preferred).  To
  cite an individual counterexample, give its result id -- for example
  aim-problem-35 -- which is stable across revisions and is what registry.json
  enumerates.  Ledger numbers are presentation order and are not stable.  The
  uid on each registry row is a database key, not a citation.
title: "count-ex-machina: GPT, the Counterexample Machine"
abstract: >-
  An archive of AI-assisted counterexamples to published conjectures and to
  formally posed problems, admitted only with independently checkable
  certificates: every case is verified by exact arithmetic or by a rigorous
  interval computation, never by floating-point evidence alone.
type: software
